 # PowerShell Pester v6 Testing Guidelines
 
-This guide provides PowerShell-specific instructions for creating automated tests with the PowerShell Pester v6 module. Pester v6 runs on Windows PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7.4+. Follow the general PowerShell scripting guidance in [powershell.instructions.md](./powershell.instructions.md).
+> Adapted from [github/awesome-copilot](https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot)
+> `instructions/powershell-pester-6.instructions.md` (MIT, see the plugin's `LICENSE.awesome-copilot`).
+> Local fixes:
+> - removed the sentence linking to `./powershell.instructions.md`, which does not exist here;
+> - the `-TestCases` example uses the key `Value` instead of `Input`: `$Input` is an automatic variable, so the test failed;
+> - the `BeforeDiscovery` example uses `<_.Name>` and `$_.Name`: `ConvertFrom-Json` yields objects, not hashtables, so `$Name` was `$null` and the test passed vacuously;
+> - the structure skeleton puts each `{ # comment }` on its own line; on one line the comment hides the closing brace.
+
+This guide provides PowerShell-specific instructions for creating automated tests with the PowerShell Pester v6 module. Pester v6 runs on Windows PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7.4+.
 
 Pester v6 is largely compatible with v5, but it makes several previously deprecated behaviours fail fast. Keep each test file self-contained and run the suite with the same PowerShell and Pester versions used by CI.
 
